9. Macro‑Action Consistency and Two‑Timescale Decomposition

A macro‑action \mu is a deterministic sequence of primitive contacts and low‑level controllers of duration L_\mu. The macro‑action MDP has value function V_{\text{macro}}^*.

Theorem 7 (Macro‑Action Consistency).
If the macro‑action library \mathcal{M} contains all primitive contact sequences of length up to L_{\max}, then V_{\text{macro}}^* = V^* and the greedy macro‑action policy achieves V^*.

Proof. The macro‑action Bellman operator coincides with the L-step primitive operator; both share the same unique fixed point. ∎

Two‑Timescale FCV. Offline, a library of macro‑actions is computed with exact LCP dynamics using the IMPACT solver (2026); online, the robot uses complementarity‑free CI‑MPC (reduced‑order guided, 2025) with relaxation error \delta_{\text{cf}}. Let P^* be the true transition kernel and \widehat P the approximate kernel; assume \|P^* - \widehat P\|_{\text{TV}} \le \delta_{\text{cf}} uniformly, and that the value function is L_V-Lipschitz with respect to the state distribution in total variation.

Theorem 8 (Offline‑Online Gap).
Let V^{\text{offline}} and V^{\text{online}} be the optimal values under exact and approximate dynamics. Then

|V^{\text{offline}} - V^{\text{online}}| \;\le\; \frac{\gamma L_V}{1-\gamma}\, \delta_{\text{cf}}.

Proof. By definition, V^{\text{offline}} = r + \gamma P^* V^{\text{offline}} and V^{\text{online}} = r + \gamma \widehat P V^{\text{online}}. Subtracting,

\|V^{\text{offline}} - V^{\text{online}}\|_\infty \le \gamma \|P^* V^{\text{offline}} - \widehat P V^{\text{online}}\|_\infty \le \gamma \|V^{\text{offline}} - V^{\text{online}}\|_\infty + \gamma L_V \delta_{\text{cf}},

from which the bound follows. ∎

