Appendix B. Proof of Theorem 2 (Wasserstein Robust FCV Bound)

Theorem 2. Let \hat p(\cdot \mid b,c,a) be the nominal transition, and \mathfrak{P}(b,c,a) = \{ p \mid W_\rho(p,\hat p) \le \epsilon \}. If V^* is L-Lipschitz with respect to W_1 (hence any W_\rho, \rho\ge 1), then

\operatorname{FCV}_{\text{rob}}(b,c) \ge \operatorname{FCV}_{\text{nom}}(b,c) - \gamma L \epsilon .

Proof. For any fixed a, the Kantorovich–Rubinstein duality for W_1 (Lemma J.3) gives

\inf_{p:\,W_1(p,\hat p)\le\epsilon} \mathbb{E}_{p}[V^*] \ge \mathbb{E}_{\hat p}[V^*] - L\epsilon .

Since W_\rho \ge W_1 for \rho\ge 1, the W_\rho ambiguity set is a subset of the W_1 ball of the same radius, so the bound remains valid. Substituting into the definition of \operatorname{FCV}_{\text{rob}},

\begin{aligned}
\operatorname{FCV}_{\text{rob}}(b,c) 
&= \max_{a} \Bigl( r(b,c,a) + \gamma \inf_{p\in\mathfrak{P}} \mathbb{E}_{p}[V^*] \Bigr) - V^*(b) \\
&\ge \max_{a} \bigl( r + \gamma \mathbb{E}_{\hat p}[V^*] - \gamma L \epsilon \bigr) - V^*(b) \\
&= \bigl( \max_{a}(r + \gamma \mathbb{E}_{\hat p}[V^*]) - V^*(b) \bigr) - \gamma L \epsilon \\
&= \operatorname{FCV}_{\text{nom}}(b,c) - \gamma L \epsilon .
\end{aligned}

\square

