Appendix C. Proof of Theorem 3 (Value of Information Lower Bound)

Theorem 3. Assume state factorises X = (X_r, \mathcal{M}) with independent priors, and that for every contact c and belief b there exists at least one observation with D_{\text{KL}} > 0 and V^*(b') > V^*(b) (non‑degenerate observations). Define

\kappa_{\text{ext}} = \inf_{b,\,z_{\text{ext}}:\,D_{\text{KL}}>0} \frac{V^*(b^{\mathcal{M},z_{\text{ext}}}) - V^*(b)}{D_{\text{KL}}(b^{\mathcal{M},z_{\text{ext}}} \| b^{\mathcal{M}})}, \qquad
\kappa_{\text{prop}} = \inf_{b,\,z_{\text{prop}}:\,D_{\text{KL}}>0} \frac{V^*(b^{X_r,z_{\text{prop}}}) - V^*(b)}{D_{\text{KL}}(b^{X_r,z_{\text{prop}}} \| b^{X_r})}.

Then for any contact c,

\mathbb{E}[V^*(b'_c)] - \mathbb{E}[V^*(b'_0)] \ge \kappa_{\text{ext}} I(\mathcal{M}; Z_{\text{ext}} \mid b,c) + \kappa_{\text{prop}} I(X_r; Z_{\text{prop}} \mid b,c, \mathcal{M}).

Proof. By definition of \kappa_{\text{ext}} as an infimum over all reachable posterior beliefs after a single observation, for any z_{\text{ext}} that yields a positive information gain we have

V^*(b^{\mathcal{M},z_{\text{ext}}}) - V^*(b^{\mathcal{M}}) \ge \kappa_{\text{ext}} \, D_{\text{KL}}(b^{\mathcal{M},z_{\text{ext}}} \| b^{\mathcal{M}}).

Taking the expectation over z_{\text{ext}} gives

\mathbb{E}_{z_{\text{ext}}}[V^*(b^{\mathcal{M},z_{\text{ext}}})] - V^*(b^{\mathcal{M}}) \ge \kappa_{\text{ext}} \, I(\mathcal{M}; Z_{\text{ext}} \mid b,c).

Because the exteroceptive observation z_{\text{ext}} does not alter the marginal belief over X_r (the prior is independent), this inequality extends to the full belief b. The proprioceptive part follows analogously, conditioning on the true environment \mathcal{M}. Summing the two terms yields the claimed bound. \square

